# AR Ketelhuis Steyl

AR Ketelhuis Steyl is a Unity AR prototype made for a school/client project at Fontys. The goal of the project is to explore how AR can be used to create an interactive educational experience for the Ketelhuis in Steyl.

The prototype focuses on placing and interacting with AR objects on a tablet. One of the main interactions is a valve mechanic where the user turns a virtual valve to affect the state of the experience.

## Context

This project was made during my HBO-ICT study at Fontys University of Applied Sciences. The project was connected to the Ketelhuis in Steyl, where the goal was to design an educational experience for primary school pupils.

## My contribution

I worked on the Unity AR prototype and focused on testing basic AR interaction. I set up AR Foundation, plane detection, object placement, and a first valve interaction prototype.

## Features

- AR plane detection
- Tap-to-place interaction
- Interactive valve prototype
- Visual feedback through object state changes
- Unity tablet build testing

## Tech stack

- Unity
- AR Foundation
- ARCore
- C#

## Current status

This project is still a prototype. The main goal was to validate basic AR placement and interaction before developing a more complete educational experience.

